le=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>mirtCAT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mirt_object </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mm2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MAP&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> criteria </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Drule&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> start_item </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> local_pattern </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dat_imput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>My problem is that I got the following error message after running the mirtCAT function:<br><br><b>&quot;Error in FI(extract.item(MCE$test$mirt_object, x), Theta = thetas) : Fisher-information matrix not currently supported for supplied classes&quot;</b><br><br>Replacing the item selection criterion by &quot;KL&quot; solves the problem, but 