     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Le vendredi 12 décembre 2014 17:12:28 UTC+1, Phil Chalmers a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Pierre,<span><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Dec 12, 2014 at 10:42 AM, Pierre Michel <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">aliasj...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Phil,<br><br>I fitted a multidimensional GPCM to my data using the mirt package, I estimated factor scores a first time. Then, in order to have complete response patterns (to perform CAT simualtions), I imputed the data and refitted the same model. Then I could run the mirtCAT function with all these outputs (here I generate a CAT using the first observation of my imputed data). Here is the corresponding script:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fscores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MAP&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> full</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><br><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">dat_imput </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> imputeMissing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scores</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code><br><br>mm2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat_imput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gpcm&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">MAXQUAD </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>mirtCAT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mirt_object </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mm2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MAP&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> criteria </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Drule&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> start_item </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> local_pattern </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dat_imput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>My problem is that I got the following error message after running the mirtCAT function:<br><br><b>&quot;Error in FI(extract.item(MCE$test$mirt_<u></u>object, x), Theta = thetas